From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 09:56:41 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: correct stale per-port resource-map comments

Six comments in the two files this series touches document maps the code
next to them contradicts. They all predate the correction of the LAN port
resource derivation, which was forced by two symptoms on hardware: eth0
placed on dequeue port 7 egressed the dp2/LAN4 channel, and TMU egress
port 15 drained to a dequeue port no DMA puller was attached to. The
closed forms have been

  cbm_deq_port == tmu_egress_port == dp_port_id + 5
  tmu_queue    == dp_port_id + 15

ever since; only the prose lagged.

Corrected: the TMU resource table in cbm_dp.c (EPN 12..15 / QID 22..25
-> EPN 7..10 / QID 17..20, with the SBIDs added since the probe path now
derives them); cbm_dp_port_alloc()'s field contract, which still said
"deq_port = port_id + 2"; a parenthetical claiming
"tmu_egress_port = dp_port_id + 10"; and the mapping table in
intel_xrx500.c (deq 7/6/5/4, EPN 15..12). The derivation note that
followed that last table -- reasoning from the 5.10 device tree's
interrupt-names "cbm-dqm4".."cbm-dqm7" to DQ ports 4..7 running inversely
against dp_port_id -- was the origin of the error, so it goes rather than
being patched.

Two more that this series itself falsified: cbm_dp_enable()'s
preconfig-skip note still said "dp5/eth0 is preconfigured at probe;
dp2..4 build here as before", which stopped being true when the probe
loop was extended to all four ports (the gated block is now dead for
every LAN port, and the comment explains why keeping the gate is still
right); and intel_xrx500's TX-init note said ltq_dma_chan_desc_alloc()
"stashes vaddr in pch->desc_base", which has been the CKSEG1 alias of the
ring's physical address since the descriptor-vaddr fix earlier in this
series.

Comments only, no code change.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_dp.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_dp.c
index 2c41ac2ff6e1..9117d87c9194 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/cqm/grx500/cbm_dp.c
@@ -38,16 +38,18 @@
  * @port_id: CBM port (caller-supplied; 0..15 fits the 0xF0 mask).
  *
  * dp_port_id 2..5 -> { tmu_egress_port (EPN), tmu_queue (QID) }. The EPN is
- * dp_port_id + 10 (12..15, matching intel_xrx500.c:1941 port->tmu_egress_port
- * and the AVM-orientation table). The QID is taken from the AVM
- * xrx500_cbm_config[] DMA-port table (cbm_config.c): tmu_port 12..15 carry
- * tmu_queue 22..25. SBID_START=16 (AVM cbm.h:207) -> base_sbid = tmu_queue -
- * 16.
+ * dp_port_id + 5 and the QID is dp_port_id + 15, per AVM's epg_lookup_table
+ * and the xrx500_cbm_config[] DQ7..DQ10 rows; the EPN equals the CBM dequeue
+ * port, because AVM's conf_dqm_dma_port passes the same number to
+ * tmu_create_flat_egress_path and init_cbm_dqm_dma_port. SBID_START=16 (AVM
+ * cbm.h:207) -> base_sbid = tmu_queue - 16.
  *
- *   dp 2 -> EPN 12, QID 22   (eth3 / LAN4)
- *   dp 3 -> EPN 13, QID 23   (eth2 / LAN3)
- *   dp 4 -> EPN 14, QID 24   (eth1 / LAN2)
- *   dp 5 -> EPN 15, QID 25   (eth0 / LAN1)
+ *   dp 2 -> EPN  7, QID 17, SBID 1   (eth3 / LAN4)
+ *   dp 3 -> EPN  8, QID 18, SBID 2   (eth2 / LAN3)
+ *   dp 4 -> EPN  9, QID 19, SBID 3   (eth1 / LAN2)
+ *   dp 5 -> EPN 10, QID 20, SBID 4   (eth0 / LAN1)
+ *
+ * The code below has been on the +5/+15 form since; only this comment lagged.
  */
 
 static u32 cbm_dp_tmu_egress_port(int port_id)
